{"id":"mahabharata-3-082","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":82,"title":"द्व्यशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 82 · Fords of the east: Gaya and beyond","summary":{"en":"Pulastya continues with Dharmatirtha, Gaya with its undying banyan where offerings to the ancestors last forever, Prayaga, the Ganga and many more fords and their rewards.","kn":"ಧರ್ಮತೀರ್ಥ, ಪಿತೃಗಳಿಗೆ ಕೊಟ್ಟ ದಾನ ಅಕ್ಷಯವಾಗುವ ಅಕ್ಷಯವಟವಿರುವ ಗಯಾ, ಪ್ರಯಾಗ, ಗಂಗೆ ಮತ್ತು ಇನ್ನೂ ಅನೇಕ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳನ್ನೂ ಅವುಗಳ ಫಲವನ್ನೂ ಪುಲಸ್ತ್ಯರು ಮುಂದುವರಿಸಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"पुलस्त्य धर्मतीर्थ, अक्षयवट वाले गया, जहाँ पितरों को दिया दान अक्षय होता है, प्रयाग, गंगा और अनेक अन्य तीर्थों तथा उनके फलों का वर्णन जारी रखते हैं।","te":"ధర్మతీర్థం, పితరులకు ఇచ్చిన దానం అక్షయమయ్యే అక్షయవటం ఉన్న గయ, ప్రయాగ, గంగ, ఇంకా అనేక తీర్థాలను, వాటి ఫలాలను పులస్త్యుడు కొనసాగించి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"தர்மதீர்த்தம், முன்னோர்களுக்கு அளிக்கும் தானம் அழியாததாகும் அக்ஷயவடம் உள்ள கயை, ப்ரயாகை, கங்கை மற்றும் பல தீர்த்தங்களையும் அவற்றின் பலன்களையும் புலஸ்த்யர் தொடர்ந்து சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"ധർമ്മതീർത്ഥം, എന്നും നിലനിൽക്കുന്ന ആൽമരമുള്ള ഗയ എന്നിവിടങ്ങളിൽ പിതൃക്കൾക്കുള്ള ബലികൾ ശാശ്വതമായി ഫലം നൽകുന്നു. പ്രയാഗ, ഗംഗ, മറ്റ് പല തീർത്ഥങ്ങളും അവയുടെ ഫലങ്ങളും പുലസ്ത്യൻ തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.82; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"पुलस्त्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pulastya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो गच्छेत धर्मज्ञ धर्मतीर्थं पुरातनम् ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरो राजन्धर्मशीलः समाहितः ।\nआसप्तमं कुलं राजन्पुनीते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knower of dharma, one should go to the ancient Dharmatirtha; a man of righteous character who bathes there with composed mind purifies his family to the seventh generation, without doubt."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो गच्छेत धर्मज्ञ कारापतनमुत्तमम् ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति मुनिलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knower of dharma, one should go to the excellent Karapatana; one gains the Agnishtoma and goes to the sages' world."}},{"n":3,"text":"सौगन्धिकं वनं राजंस्ततो गच्छेत मानवः ।\nयत्र ब्रह्मादयो देवा ऋषयश्च तपोधनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, one should go to the forest Saugandhika, where Brahma and other gods and ascetic sages,"}},{"n":4,"text":"सिद्धचारणगन्धर्वाः किंनराः समहोरगाः ।\nतद्वनं प्रविशन्नेव सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"siddhas, charanas, gandharvas, kinnaras and great serpents dwell; merely by entering that forest one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो हि सा सरिच्छ्रेष्ठा नदीनामुत्तमा नदी ।\nप्लक्षाद्देवी स्रुता राजन्महापुण्या सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king, the divine Sarasvati, best of rivers and very holy, flows out from a plaksha tree."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वीत वल्मीकान्निःसृते जले ।\nअर्चयित्वा पितॄन्देवानश्वमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should bathe there in the water that comes from an ant-hill, and by honouring ancestors and gods gain the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":7,"text":"ईशानाध्युषितं नाम तत्र तीर्थं सुदुर्लभम् ।\nषट्सु शम्यानिपातेषु वल्मीकादिति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a very rare ford named Ishanadhyushita, fixed at six bowshots from the ant-hill."}},{"n":8,"text":"कपिलानां सहस्रं च वाजिमेधं च विन्दति ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरव्याघ्र दृष्टमेतत्पुरातने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there, tiger among men, one gains a thousand tawny cows and the horse sacrifice; this was seen in ancient times."}},{"n":9,"text":"सुगन्धां शतकुम्भां च पञ्चयज्ञां च भारत ।\nअभिगम्य नरश्रेष्ठ स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Sugandha, Shatakumbha and Panchayajna, best of men, one is honoured in heaven."}},{"n":10,"text":"त्रिशूलखातं तत्रैव तीर्थमासाद्य भारत ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कुर्वीत पितृदेवार्चने रतः ।\nगाणपत्यं स लभते देहं त्यक्त्वा न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the ford Trishulakhata there, O Bharata, one should bathe, devoted to honouring ancestors and gods; on leaving the body he gains leadership of Shiva's host, without doubt."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र देव्याः स्थानं सुदुर्लभम् ।\nशाकंभरीति विख्याता त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the very rare place of the Goddess, famed in the three worlds as Shakambhari."}},{"n":12,"text":"दिव्यं वर्षसहस्रं हि शाकेन किल सुव्रत ।\nआहारं सा कृतवती मासि मासि नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a divine thousand years, they say, good vower, she lived on vegetables month after month, O lord of men."}},{"n":13,"text":"ऋषयोऽभ्यागतास्तत्र देव्या भक्त्या तपोधनाः ।\nआतिथ्यं च कृतं तेषां शाकेन किल भारत ।\nततः शाकम्भरीत्येव नाम तस्याः प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sages rich in austerity came there out of devotion to the Goddess, and she is said to have hosted them with vegetables, O Bharata. Hence her name Shakambhari was established."}},{"n":14,"text":"शाकंभरीं समासाद्य ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nत्रिरात्रमुषितः शाकं भक्षयेन्नियतः शुचिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Shakambhari, a celibate with composed mind should stay three nights and eat vegetables, restrained and pure."}},{"n":15,"text":"शाकाहारस्य यत्सम्यग्वर्षैर्द्वादशभिः फलम् ।\nतत्फलं तस्य भवति देव्याश्छन्देन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fruit that comes from living properly on vegetables for twelve years comes to him at the Goddess's pleasure, O Bharata."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो गच्छेत्सुवर्णाक्षं त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतम् ।\nयत्र विष्णुः प्रसादार्थं रुद्रमाराधयत्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Suvarnaksha, famed in the three worlds, where Vishnu once worshipped Rudra to win his favour."}},{"n":17,"text":"वरांश्च सुबहूँल्लेभे दैवतेषु सुदुर्लभान् ।\nउक्तश्च त्रिपुरघ्नेन परितुष्टेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He received very many boons rare even among the gods. The pleased destroyer of Tripura said to him, O Bharata:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अपि चास्मत्प्रियतरो लोके कृष्ण भविष्यसि ।\nत्वन्मुखं च जगत्कृत्स्नं भविष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, you will be dearer to us than anyone in the world, and the whole world will come to be within your face, without doubt.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्राभिगम्य राजेन्द्र पूजयित्वा वृषध्वजम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति गाणपत्यं च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there and worshipping the bull-bannered god, O king of kings, one gains the horse sacrifice and leadership of Shiva's host."}},{"n":20,"text":"धूमावतीं ततो गच्छेत्त्रिरत्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nमनसा प्रार्थितान्कामाँल्लभते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after fasting three nights, one should go to Dhumavati; one gains the desires one wishes in the mind, without doubt."}},{"n":21,"text":"देव्यास्तु दक्षिणार्धेन रथावर्तो नराधिप ।\nतत्रारोहेत धर्मज्ञ श्रद्दधानो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nमहादेवप्रसादाद्धि गच्छेत परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the southern half of the Goddess's place, ruler of men, is Rathavarta; a knower of dharma with faith and restrained senses should climb it, and by Mahadeva's grace reaches the highest goal."}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य गच्छेत भरतर्षभ ।\nधारां नाम महाप्राज्ञ सर्वपापप्रणाशिनीम् ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरव्याघ्र न शोचति नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"After circling it, best of the Bharatas, one should go to the stream named Dhara, wise one, which destroys all sins. Bathing there, tiger among men, one does not grieve, O king."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो गच्छेत धर्मज्ञ नमस्कृत्य महागिरिम् ।\nस्वर्गद्वारेण यत्तुल्यं गङ्गाद्वारं न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knower of dharma, after bowing to the great mountain, one should go to Gangadvara, which is certainly equal to the gate of heaven."}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वीत कोटितीर्थे समाहितः ।\nपुण्डरीकमवाप्नोति कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should bathe there at Kotitirtha with composed mind; one gains the Pundarika sacrifice and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":25,"text":"सप्तगङ्गे त्रिगङ्गे च शक्रावर्ते च तर्पयन् ।\nदेवान्पितॄंश्च विधिवत्पुण्यलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Offering water to gods and ancestors by the rules at Saptaganga, Triganga and Shakravarta, one is honoured in the world of the righteous."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः कनखले स्नात्वा त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, bathing at Kanakhala and fasting three nights, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to heaven."}},{"n":27,"text":"कपिलावटं च गच्छेत तीर्थसेवी नराधिप ।\nउष्यैकां रजनीं तत्र गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pilgrim should go to Kapilavata, ruler of men; staying one night there, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":28,"text":"नागराजस्य राजेन्द्र कपिलस्य महात्मनाः ।\nतीर्थं कुरुवरश्रेष्ठ सर्वलोकेषु विश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Kurus, king of kings, there is the ford of the serpent king, the great soul Kapila, famed in all the worlds."}},{"n":29,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वीत नागतीर्थे नराधिप ।\nकपिलानां सहस्रस्य फलं प्राप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should bathe there at Nagatirtha, ruler of men; a man gains the fruit of a thousand tawny cows."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो ललितिकां गच्छेच्छंतनोस्तीर्थमुत्तमम् ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरो राजन्न दुर्गतिमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Lalitika, Shantanu's excellent ford; bathing there, O king, one meets no evil fate."}},{"n":31,"text":"गङ्गासंगमयोश्चैव स्नाति यः संगमे नरः ।\nदशाश्वमेधानाप्नोति कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who bathes at the confluence of the Ganga and the Sangama gains ten horse sacrifices and uplifts his family."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र सुगन्धां लोकविश्रुताम् ।\nसर्वपापविशुद्धात्मा ब्रह्मलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the world-famed Sugandha; with the self cleansed of all sins, one is honoured in Brahma's world."}},{"n":33,"text":"रुद्रावर्तं ततो गच्छेत्तीर्थसेवी नराधिप ।\nतत्र स्नात्वा नरो राजन्स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the pilgrim should go to Rudravarta, ruler of men; bathing there, O king, one is honoured in heaven."}},{"n":34,"text":"गङ्गायाश्च नरश्रेष्ठ सरस्वत्याश्च संगमे ।\nस्नातोऽश्वमेधमाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes at the confluence of the Ganga and the Sarasvati, best of men, gains the horse sacrifice and goes to heaven."}},{"n":35,"text":"भद्रकर्णेश्वरं गत्वा देवमर्च्य यथाविधि ।\nन दुर्गतिमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Bhadrakarneshvara and worshipping the god by the rules, one meets no evil fate and goes to heaven."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः कुब्जाम्रकं गच्छेत्तीर्थसेवी यथाक्रमम् ।\nगोसहस्रमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the pilgrim, in order, should go to Kubjamraka; he gains a thousand cows and goes to heaven."}},{"n":37,"text":"अरुन्धतीवटं गच्छेत्तीर्थसेवी नराधिप ।\nसामुद्रकमुपस्पृश्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nगोसहस्रफलं विन्देत्कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pilgrim, ruler of men, should go to Arundhativata; rinsing at Samudraka and fasting three nights, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":38,"text":"ब्रह्मावर्तं ततो गच्छेद्ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a celibate with composed mind should go to Brahmavarta; he gains the horse sacrifice and goes to heaven."}},{"n":39,"text":"यमुनाप्रभवं गत्वा उपस्पृश्य च यामुने ।\nअश्वमेधफलं लब्ध्वा स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to the source of the Yamuna and rinsing the mouth in the Yamuna, one gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice and is honoured in heaven."}},{"n":40,"text":"दर्वीसंक्रमणं प्राप्य तीर्थं त्रैलोक्यविश्रुतम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Darvisankramana, a ford famed in the three worlds, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to heaven."}},{"n":41,"text":"सिन्धोश्च प्रभवं गत्वा सिद्धगन्धर्वसेवितम् ।\nतत्रोष्य रजनीः पञ्च विन्द्याद्बहु सुवर्णकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to the source of the Sindhu, frequented by siddhas and gandharvas, and staying five nights there, one gains much gold."}},{"n":42,"text":"अथ वेदीं समासाद्य नरः परमदुर्गमाम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति गच्छेच्चौशनसीं गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the very hard-to-reach Vedi, a man gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Ushanas's state."}},{"n":43,"text":"ऋषिकुल्यां समासाद्य वासिष्ठं चैव भारत ।\nवासिष्ठं समतिक्रम्य सर्वे वर्णा द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Rishikulya and Vasishtha, O Bharata, and passing beyond Vasishtha, all the twice-born classes,"}},{"n":44,"text":"ऋषिकुल्यां नरः स्नात्वा ऋषिलोकं प्रपद्यते ।\nयदि तत्र वसेन्मासं शाकाहारो नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"a man who bathes at Rishikulya reaches the sages' world; and if he lives there a month on a vegetable diet, O ruler of men,"}},{"n":45,"text":"भृगुतुङ्गं समासाद्य वाजिमेधफलं लभेत् ।\nगत्वा वीरप्रमोक्षं च सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"and reaches Bhriguttunga, he gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice. Going to Viramokha, he is freed from all sins."}},{"n":46,"text":"कृत्तिकामघयोश्चैव तीर्थमासाद्य भारत ।\nअग्निष्टोमातिरात्राभ्यां फलं प्राप्नोति पुण्यकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the ford of Krittika and Magha, O Bharata, a man of merit gains the fruit of the Agnishtoma and Atiratra."}},{"n":47,"text":"ततः संध्यां समासाद्य विद्यातीर्थमनुत्तमम् ।\nउपस्पृश्य च विद्यानां सर्वासां पारगो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Sandhya and the unsurpassed Vidyatirtha, and rinsing there, one becomes master of all the sciences."}},{"n":48,"text":"महाश्रमे वसेद्रात्रिं सर्वपापप्रमोचने ।\nएककालं निराहारो लोकानावसते शुभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At Mahashrama, which frees from all sins, one should stay a night; eating once a day, one dwells in auspicious worlds."}},{"n":49,"text":"षष्ठकालोपवासेन मासमुष्य महालये ।\nसर्वपापविशुद्धात्मा विन्द्याद्बहु सुवर्णकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Staying a month at Mahalaya, taking food only at the sixth mealtime, with the self cleansed of all sin, one gains much gold."}},{"n":50,"text":"अथ वेतसिकां गत्वा पितामहनिषेविताम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति गच्छेच्चौशनसीं गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Vetasika, frequented by the Grandfather, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Ushanas's state."}},{"n":51,"text":"अथ सुन्दरिकातीर्थं प्राप्य सिद्धनिषेवितम् ।\nरूपस्य भागी भवति दृष्टमेतत्पुरातने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the ford Sundarika, frequented by siddhas, one gains beauty; this was seen in ancient times."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततो वै ब्राह्मणीं गत्वा ब्रह्मचारी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nपद्मवर्णेन यानेन ब्रह्मलोकं प्रपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Brahmani, a celibate who has mastered his senses reaches Brahma's world in a lotus-hued chariot."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततश्च नैमिषं गच्छेत्पुण्यं सिद्धनिषेवितम् ।\nतत्र नित्यं निवसति ब्रह्मा देवगणैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to holy Naimisha, frequented by siddhas, where Brahma always dwells surrounded by hosts of gods."}},{"n":54,"text":"नैमिषं प्रार्थयानस्य पापस्यार्धं प्रणश्यति ।\nप्रविष्टमात्रस्तु नरः सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who merely wishes for Naimisha, half his sin is destroyed; merely by entering it a man is freed from all sins."}},{"n":55,"text":"तत्र मासं वसेद्धीरो नैमिषे तीर्थतत्परः ।\nपृथिव्यां यानि तीर्थानि नैमिषे तानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A steadfast pilgrim should stay a month at Naimisha. All the fords on earth are at Naimisha, O Bharata."}},{"n":56,"text":"अभिषेककृतस्तत्र नियतो नियताशनः ।\nगवामयस्य यज्ञस्य फलं प्राप्नोति भारत ।\nपुनात्यासप्तमं चैव कुलं भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes there, restrained and with restrained diet, gains the fruit of the Gavamaya sacrifice, O Bharata, and purifies his family to the seventh generation, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":57,"text":"यस्त्यजेन्नैमिषे प्राणानुपवासपरायणः ।\nस मोदेत्स्वर्गलोकस्थ एवमाहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nनित्यं पुण्यं च मेध्यं च नैमिषं नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives up his life at Naimisha, devoted to fasting, rejoices in heaven; so the wise say. Naimisha is always holy and pure, best of kings."}},{"n":58,"text":"गङ्गोद्भेदं समासाद्य त्रिरात्रोपोषितो नरः ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति ब्रह्मभूतश्च जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Gangodbheda and fasting three nights, a man gains the Vajapeya and is born as one who has become Brahman."}},{"n":59,"text":"सरस्वतीं समासाद्य तर्पयेत्पितृदेवताः ।\nसारस्वतेषु लोकेषु मोदते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the Sarasvati and offering water to ancestors and gods, he rejoices in the worlds of the Sarasvata, without doubt."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततश्च बाहुदां गच्छेद्ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nदेवसत्रस्य यज्ञस्य फलं प्राप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a celibate with composed mind should go to the Bahuda; a man gains the fruit of the Devasatra sacrifice."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततश्चीरवतीं गच्छेत्पुण्यां पुण्यतमैर्वृताम् ।\nपितृदेवार्चनरतो वाजपेयमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to the holy Chiravati, surrounded by the very holy; devoted to honouring ancestors and gods, one gains the Vajapeya."}},{"n":62,"text":"विमलाशोकमासाद्य विराजति यथा शशी ।\nतत्रोष्य रजनीमेकां स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Vimalashoka, one shines like the moon; staying a night there, one is honoured in heaven."}},{"n":63,"text":"गोप्रतारं ततो गच्छेत्सरय्वास्तीर्थमुत्तमम् ।\nयत्र रामो गतः स्वर्गं सभृत्यबलवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Gopratara, the Sarayu's excellent ford, where Rama went to heaven with his servants, army and vehicles."}},{"n":64,"text":"देहं त्यक्त्वा दिवं यातस्तस्य तीर्थस्य तेजसा ।\nरामस्य च प्रसादेन व्यवसायाच्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving his body he went to heaven by that ford's power, by Rama's grace and by his own resolve, O Bharata."}},{"n":65,"text":"तस्मिंस्तीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा गोप्रतारे नराधिप ।\nसर्वपापविशुद्धात्मा स्वर्गलोके महीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who bathes at that ford, Gopratara, ruler of men, has his self cleansed of all sin and is honoured in heaven."}},{"n":66,"text":"रामतीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा गोमत्यां कुरुनन्दन ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति पुनाति च कुलं नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at Ramatirtha on the Gomati, joy of the Kurus, a man gains the horse sacrifice and purifies his family."}},{"n":67,"text":"शतसाहस्रिकं तत्र तीर्थं भरतसत्तम ।\nतत्रोपस्पर्शनं कृत्वा नियतो नियताशनः ।\nगोसहस्रफलं पुण्यं प्राप्नोति भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a ford called Shatasahasrika there, best of the Bharatas; rinsing there, restrained and with restrained diet, one gains the holy fruit of a thousand cows, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":68,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र भर्तृस्थानमनुत्तमम् ।\nकोटितीर्थे नरः स्नात्वा अर्चयित्वा गुहं नृप ।\nगोसहस्रफलं विन्देत्तेजस्वी च भवेन्नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the unsurpassed Bhartristhana; bathing at Kotitirtha and worshipping Guha, O king, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows and becomes radiant."}},{"n":69,"text":"ततो वाराणसीं गत्वा अर्चयित्वा वृषध्वजम् ।\nकपिलाह्रदे नरः स्नात्वा राजसूयफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Varanasi and worshipping the bull-bannered god, a man who bathes at Kapilahrada gains the fruit of the Rajasuya."}},{"n":70,"text":"मार्कण्डेयस्य राजेन्द्र तीर्थमासाद्य दुर्लभम् ।\nगोमतीगङ्गयोश्चैव संगमे लोकविश्रुते ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Markandeya's rare ford, king of kings, and the world-famed confluence of the Gomati and Ganga, one gains the Agnishtoma and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":71,"text":"ततो गयां समासाद्य ब्रह्मचारी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति गमनादेव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Gaya, a celibate who has mastered his senses gains the horse sacrifice merely by going there, O Bharata."}},{"n":72,"text":"तत्राक्षयवटो नाम त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतः ।\nपितॄणां तत्र वै दत्तमक्षयं भवति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the Akshayavata, famed in the three worlds; whatever is given there to the ancestors becomes imperishable, lord."}},{"n":73,"text":"महानद्यामुपस्पृश्य तर्पयेत्पितृदेवताः ।\nअक्षयान्प्राप्नुयाल्लोकान्कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rinsing in the Mahanadi and offering water to ancestors and gods, one gains imperishable worlds and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":74,"text":"ततो ब्रह्मसरो गच्छेद्धर्मारण्योपशोभितम् ।\nपौण्डरीकमवाप्नोति प्रभातामेव शर्वरीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Brahmasara, adorned by Dharmaranya; one gains the Pundarika sacrifice by spending even a night until dawn."}},{"n":75,"text":"तस्मिन्सरसि राजेन्द्र ब्रह्मणो यूप उच्छ्रितः ।\nयूपं प्रदक्षिणं कृत्वा वाजपेयफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the bank of that lake, king of kings, Brahma's sacrificial post stands raised; after circling the post one gains the fruit of the Vajapeya."}},{"n":76,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र धेनुकां लोकविश्रुताम् ।\nएकरात्रोषितो राजन्प्रयच्छेत्तिलधेनुकाम् ।\nसर्वपापविशुद्धात्मा सोमलोकं व्रजेद्ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the world-famed Dhenuka. After staying a night there, O king, one should give a cow made of sesame; with the self cleansed of all sin, one surely goes to the moon's world."}},{"n":77,"text":"तत्र चिह्नं महाराज अद्यापि हि न संशयः ।\nकपिला सह वत्सेन पर्वते विचरत्युत ।\nसवत्सायाः पदानि स्म दृश्यन्तेऽद्यापि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a sign there even today, great king, without doubt: a tawny cow roams the mountain with her calf, and the footprints of the cow and calf are seen there even now, O Bharata."}},{"n":78,"text":"तेषूपस्पृश्य राजेन्द्र पदेषु नृपसत्तम ।\nयत्किंचिदशुभं कर्म तत्प्रणश्यति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rinsing at those footprints, king of kings, best of kings, whatever inauspicious deed one has done is destroyed, O Bharata."}},{"n":79,"text":"ततो गृध्रवटं गच्छेत्स्थानं देवस्य धीमतः ।\nस्नायीत भस्मना तत्र अभिगम्य वृषध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Gridhravata, the place of the wise god; going to the bull-bannered god there, one should bathe in ashes."}},{"n":80,"text":"ब्राह्मणेन भवेच्चीर्णं व्रतं द्वादशवार्षिकम् ।\nइतरेषां तु वर्णानां सर्वपापं प्रणश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a brahmin the twelve-year vow is thus completed; for the other classes all sin is destroyed."}},{"n":81,"text":"गच्छेत तत उद्यन्तं पर्वतं गीतनादितम् ।\nसावित्रं तु पदं तत्र दृश्यते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to the Udyanta mountain, resounding with song, where Savitri's footprint is seen, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":82,"text":"तत्र संध्यामुपासीत ब्राह्मणः संशितव्रतः ।\nउपास्ता च भवेत्संध्या तेन द्वादशवार्षिकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin of sharp vows should perform the twilight prayer there; by that he is held to have performed twilight worship for twelve years."}},{"n":83,"text":"योनिद्वारं च तत्रैव विश्रुतं भरतर्षभ ।\nतत्राभिगम्य मुच्येत पुरुषो योनिसंकरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Right there is also the famed Yonidvara, best of the Bharatas; going there a man is freed from rebirth in confusion of the womb."}},{"n":84,"text":"कृष्णशुक्लावुभौ पक्षौ गयायां यो वसेन्नरः ।\nपुनात्यासप्तमं राजन्कुलं नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who lives at Gaya through both the dark and bright fortnights purifies his family to the seventh generation, O king, without doubt."}},{"n":85,"text":"एष्टव्या बहवः पुत्रा यद्येकोऽपि गयां व्रजेत् ।\nयजेत वाश्वमेधेन नीलं वा वृषमुत्सृजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many sons should be wished for, so that even one may go to Gaya, perform the horse sacrifice, or release a dark bull."}},{"n":86,"text":"ततः फल्गुं व्रजेद्राजंस्तीर्थसेवी नराधिप ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति सिद्धिं च महतीं व्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to the Phalgu, pilgrim, ruler of men; one gains the horse sacrifice and great success."}},{"n":87,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र धर्मपृष्ठं समाहितः ।\nयत्र धर्मो महाराज नित्यमास्ते युधिष्ठिर ।\nअभिगम्य ततस्तत्र वाजिमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go with composed mind to Dharmaprishtha, where Dharma always dwells, Yudhishthira; going there one gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":88,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र ब्रह्मणस्तीर्थमुत्तमम् ।\nतत्रार्चयित्वा राजेन्द्र ब्रह्माणममितौजसम् ।\nराजसूयाश्वमेधाभ्यां फलं प्राप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to Brahma's excellent ford; worshipping Brahma of boundless power there, a man gains the fruit of the Rajasuya and horse sacrifice."}},{"n":89,"text":"ततो राजगृहं गच्छेत्तीर्थसेवी नराधिप ।\nउपस्पृश्य तपोदेषु काक्षीवानिव मोदते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the pilgrim, ruler of men, should go to Rajagriha; rinsing in the hot springs, he rejoices like Kakshivan."}},{"n":90,"text":"यक्षिण्या नैत्यकं तत्र प्राश्नीत पुरुषः शुचिः ।\nयक्षिण्यास्तु प्रसादेन मुच्यते भ्रूणहत्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A pure man should eat the daily offering to the yakshini there; by the yakshini's grace he is freed from the sin of killing an embryo."}},{"n":91,"text":"मणिनागं ततो गत्वा गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ।\nनैत्यकं भुञ्जते यस्तु मणिनागस्य मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Maninaga, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows. One who eats Maninaga's daily food"}},{"n":92,"text":"दष्टस्याशीविषेणापि न तस्य क्रमते विषम् ।\nतत्रोष्य रजनीमेकां सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"is not affected by poison, even if bitten by a venomous snake. Staying one night there, one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":93,"text":"ततो गच्छेत ब्रह्मर्षेर्गौतमस्य वनं नृप ।\nअहल्याया ह्रदे स्नात्वा व्रजेत परमां गतिम् ।\nअभिगम्य श्रियं राजन्विन्दते श्रियमुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, ruler of men, one should go to the forest of the brahmin sage Gautama. Bathing in Ahalya's pool, one reaches the highest goal; going to Shri, O king, one gains supreme prosperity."}},{"n":94,"text":"तत्रोदपानो धर्मज्ञ त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतः ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कृत्वा तु वाजिमेधमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a well there, knower of dharma, famed in the three worlds; bathing there one gains the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":95,"text":"जनकस्य तु राजर्षेः कूपस्त्रिदशपूजितः ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कृत्वा तु विष्णुलोकमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The well of the royal sage Janaka is honoured by the gods; bathing there one reaches Vishnu's world."}},{"n":96,"text":"ततो विनशनं गच्छेत्सर्वपापप्रमोचनम् ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति सोमलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to Vinashana, which frees from all sins; one gains the Vajapeya and goes to the moon's world."}},{"n":97,"text":"गण्डकीं तु समासाद्य सर्वतीर्थजलोद्भवाम् ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति सूर्यलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the Gandaki, born of the waters of all fords, one gains the Vajapeya and goes to the sun's world."}},{"n":98,"text":"ततोऽधिवंश्यं धर्मज्ञ समाविश्य तपोवनम् ।\nगुह्यकेषु महाराज मोदते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knower of dharma, entering the ascetic forest of Adhivamsya, one rejoices among the guhyakas, great king, without doubt."}},{"n":99,"text":"कम्पनां तु समासाद्य नदीं सिद्धनिषेविताम् ।\nपुण्डरीकमवाप्नोति सूर्यलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the river Kampana, frequented by siddhas, one gains the Pundarika sacrifice and goes to the sun's world."}},{"n":100,"text":"ततो विशालामासाद्य नदीं त्रैलोक्यविश्रुताम् ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति स्वर्गलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the river Vishala, famed in the three worlds, one gains the Agnishtoma and goes to heaven."}},{"n":101,"text":"अथ माहेश्वरीं धारां समासाद्य नराधिप ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the Maheshvari Dhara, ruler of men, one gains the horse sacrifice and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":102,"text":"दिवौकसां पुष्करिणीं समासाद्य नरः शुचिः ।\nन दुर्गतिमवाप्नोति वाजपेयं च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A pure man who reaches the tank of the dwellers in heaven meets no evil fate and gains the Vajapeya."}},{"n":103,"text":"महेश्वरपदं गच्छेद्ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nमहेश्वरपदे स्नात्वा वाजिमेधफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A celibate with composed mind should go to Maheshvarapada; bathing there one gains the fruit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":104,"text":"तत्र कोटिस्तु तीर्थानां विश्रुता भरतर्षभ ।\nकूर्मरूपेण राजेन्द्र असुरेण दुरात्मना ।\nह्रियमाणाहृता राजन्विष्णुना प्रभविष्णुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, best of the Bharatas, a crore of fords is renowned, brought there, king, by the all-powerful Vishnu when they were being carried off by the evil asura in the form of a tortoise."}},{"n":105,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वाणस्तीर्थकोट्यां युधिष्ठिर ।\nपुण्डरीकमवाप्नोति विष्णुलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at that Tirthakoti, Yudhishthira, one gains the Pundarika sacrifice and goes to Vishnu's world."}},{"n":106,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र स्थानं नारायणस्य तु ।\nसदा संनिहितो यत्र हरिर्वसति भारत ।\nशालग्राम इति ख्यातो विष्णोरद्भुतकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to Narayana's place where Hari always dwells, known as Shalagrama, of Vishnu of wondrous deeds."}},{"n":107,"text":"अभिगम्य त्रिलोकेशं वरदं विष्णुमव्ययम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति विष्णुलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Vishnu, lord of the three worlds, giver of boons and imperishable, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Vishnu's world."}},{"n":108,"text":"तत्रोदपानो धर्मज्ञ सर्वपापप्रमोचनः ।\nसमुद्रास्तत्र चत्वारः कूपे संनिहिताः सदा ।\nतत्रोपस्पृश्य राजेन्द्र न दुर्गतिमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a well there, knower of dharma, which frees from all sins; the four oceans are always present in that well. Rinsing there, king of kings, one meets no evil fate."}},{"n":109,"text":"अभिगम्य महादेवं वरदं विष्णुमव्ययम् ।\nविराजति यथा सोम ऋणैर्मुक्तो युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Mahadeva and to Vishnu, giver of boons and imperishable, one shines like the moon, freed from debts, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":110,"text":"जातिस्मर उपस्पृश्य शुचिः प्रयतमानसः ।\nजातिस्मरत्वं प्राप्नोति स्नात्वा तत्र न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A pure man with composed mind who rinses at Jatismara gains memory of past births by bathing there, without doubt."}},{"n":111,"text":"वटेश्वरपुरं गत्वा अर्चयित्वा तु केशवम् ।\nईप्सिताँल्लभते कामानुपवासान्न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Vateshvarapura and worshipping Keshava, one gains the wished-for desires by fasting, without doubt."}},{"n":112,"text":"ततस्तु वामनं गत्वा सर्वपापप्रमोचनम् ।\nअभिवाद्य हरिं देवं न दुर्गतिमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, going to Vamana, who frees from all sins, and greeting the god Hari, one meets no evil fate."}},{"n":113,"text":"भरतस्याश्रमं गत्वा सर्वपापप्रमोचनम् ।\nकौशिकीं तत्र सेवेत महापातकनाशिनीम् ।\nराजसूयस्य यज्ञस्य फलं प्राप्नोति मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Bharata's hermitage, which frees from all sins, one should resort there to the Kaushiki, destroyer of great sins; a man gains the fruit of the Rajasuya sacrifice."}},{"n":114,"text":"ततो गच्छेत धर्मज्ञ चम्पकारण्यमुत्तमम् ।\nतत्रोष्य रजनीमेकां गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, knower of dharma, one should go to the excellent Champakaranya; staying one night there, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":115,"text":"अथ ज्येष्ठिलमासाद्य तीर्थं परमसंमतम् ।\nउपोष्य रजनीमेकामग्निष्टोमफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Jyeshthila, a ford held in the highest regard, and fasting one night, one gains the fruit of the Agnishtoma."}},{"n":116,"text":"तत्र विश्वेश्वरं दृष्ट्वा देव्या सह महाद्युतिम् ।\nमित्रावरुणयोर्लोकानाप्नोति पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vishveshvara there, of great radiance, with the Goddess, best of men, one reaches the worlds of Mitra and Varuna."}},{"n":117,"text":"कन्यासंवेद्यमासाद्य नियतो नियताशनः ।\nमनोः प्रजापतेर्लोकानाप्नोति भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Kanyasamvedya, restrained and with restrained diet, best of the Bharatas, one reaches the worlds of Manu Prajapati."}},{"n":118,"text":"कन्यायां ये प्रयच्छन्ति पानमन्नं च भारत ।\nतदक्षयमिति प्राहुरृषयः संशितव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who give drink and food to a maiden there, O Bharata, the sages of sharp vows call imperishable."}},{"n":119,"text":"निश्चीरां च समासाद्य त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुताम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति विष्णुलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Nishchira, famed in the three worlds, one gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Vishnu's world."}},{"n":120,"text":"ये तु दानं प्रयच्छन्ति निश्चीरासंगमे नराः ।\nते यान्ति नरशार्दूल ब्रह्मलोकं न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who give gifts at the confluence of the Nishchira go, tiger among men, to Brahma's world, without doubt."}},{"n":121,"text":"तत्राश्रमो वसिष्ठस्य त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुतः ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कुर्वाणो वाजपेयमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is Vasishtha's hermitage, famed in the three worlds; bathing there one gains the Vajapeya."}},{"n":122,"text":"देवकूटं समासाद्य ब्रह्मर्षिगणसेवितम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति कुलं चैव समुद्धरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Devakuta, frequented by hosts of brahmin sages, one gains the horse sacrifice and uplifts one's family."}},{"n":123,"text":"ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र कौशिकस्य मुनेर्ह्रदम् ।\nयत्र सिद्धिं परां प्राप्तो विश्वामित्रोऽथ कौशिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, one should go to the pool of the sage Kaushika, where Vishvamitra of Kushika's line attained supreme success."}},{"n":124,"text":"तत्र मासं वसेद्वीर कौशिक्यां भरतर्षभ ।\nअश्वमेधस्य यत्पुण्यं तन्मासेनाधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, one should stay a month there at the Kaushiki, best of the Bharatas; one gains in a month the merit of the horse sacrifice."}},{"n":125,"text":"सर्वतीर्थवरे चैव यो वसेत महाह्रदे ।\nन दुर्गतिमवाप्नोति विन्देद्बहु सुवर्णकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who lives at the great pool, best of all fords, meets no evil fate and gains much gold."}},{"n":126,"text":"कुमारमभिगत्वा च वीराश्रमनिवासिनम् ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति नरो नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who goes to Kumara, who lives in the Virashrama, gains the horse sacrifice, without doubt."}},{"n":127,"text":"अग्निधारां समासाद्य त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुताम् ।\nअग्निष्टोममवाप्नोति न च स्वर्गान्निवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Agnidhara, famed in the three worlds, one gains the Agnishtoma and does not return from heaven."}},{"n":128,"text":"पितामहसरो गत्वा शैलराजप्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कुर्वाणो अग्निष्टोमफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Pitamahasara, established by the king of mountains, one who bathes there gains the fruit of the Agnishtoma."}},{"n":129,"text":"पितामहस्य सरसः प्रस्रुता लोकपावनी ।\nकुमारधारा तत्रैव त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the Grandfather's lake flows the world-purifying Kumaradhara, famed in the three worlds."}},{"n":130,"text":"यत्र स्नात्वा कृतार्थोऽस्मीत्यात्मानमवगच्छति ।\nषष्ठकालोपवासेन मुच्यते ब्रह्महत्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there, one knows oneself to have fulfilled one's purpose; by fasting at the sixth mealtime one is freed from the sin of killing a brahmin."}},{"n":131,"text":"शिखरं वै महादेव्या गौर्यास्त्रैलोक्यविश्रुतम् ।\nसमारुह्य नरः श्राद्धः स्तनकुण्डेषु संविशेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing the peak of the great Goddess Gauri, famed in the three worlds, a faithful man should enter the Stanakundas."}},{"n":132,"text":"तत्राभिषेकं कुर्वाणः पितृदेवार्चने रतः ।\nहयमेधमवाप्नोति शक्रलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there, devoted to honouring ancestors and gods, he gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Indra's world."}},{"n":133,"text":"ताम्रारुणं समासाद्य ब्रह्मचारी समाहितः ।\nअश्वमेधमवाप्नोति शक्रलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Tamraruna, a celibate with composed mind gains the horse sacrifice and goes to Indra's world."}},{"n":134,"text":"नन्दिन्यां च समासाद्य कूपं त्रिदशसेवितम् ।\nनरमेधस्य यत्पुण्यं तत्प्राप्नोति कुरूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the well Nandini, frequented by the gods, one gains, joy of the Kurus, the merit of the human sacrifice."}},{"n":135,"text":"कालिकासंगमे स्नात्वा कौशिक्यारुणयोर्यतः ।\nत्रिरात्रोपोषितो विद्वान्सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The learned man who bathes at the confluence of the Kalika, where the Kaushiki and Aruna meet, and fasts three nights, is freed from all sins."}},{"n":136,"text":"उर्वशीतीर्थमासाद्य ततः सोमाश्रमं बुधः ।\nकुम्भकर्णाश्रमे स्नात्वा पूज्यते भुवि मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching Urvashitirtha and then Somashrama, the wise man who bathes at Kumbhakarna's hermitage is honoured on earth."}},{"n":137,"text":"स्नात्वा कोकामुखे पुण्ये ब्रह्मचारी यतव्रतः ।\nजातिस्मरत्वं प्राप्नोति दृष्टमेतत्पुरातने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing at holy Kokamukha, a celibate of firm vows gains memory of past births; this was seen in ancient times."}},{"n":138,"text":"सकृन्नन्दां समासाद्य कृतात्मा भवति द्विजः ।\nसर्वपापविशुद्धात्मा शक्रलोकं च गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Nanda once, a twice-born becomes accomplished in self, with the self cleansed of all sin, and goes to Indra's world."}},{"n":139,"text":"ऋषभद्वीपमासाद्य सेव्यं क्रौञ्चनिषूदनम् ।\nसरस्वत्यामुपस्पृश्य विमानस्थो विराजते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Rishabhadvipa, where the slayer of Krauncha should be served, and rinsing in the Sarasvati, one shines seated in a celestial chariot."}},{"n":140,"text":"औद्दालकं महाराज तीर्थं मुनिनिषेवितम् ।\nतत्राभिषेकं कुर्वीत सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the ford Auddalaka, great king, frequented by munis; one should bathe there and be freed from all sins."}},{"n":141,"text":"धर्मतीर्थं समासाद्य पुण्यं ब्रह्मर्षिसेवितम् ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति नरो नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the holy Dharmatirtha, frequented by brahmin sages, a man gains the Vajapeya, without doubt."}},{"n":142,"text":"तथा चम्पां समासाद्य भागीरथ्यां कृतोदकः ।\nदण्डार्कमभिगम्यैव गोसहस्रफलं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Champa and offering water in the Bhagirathi, then going to Dandarka, one gains the fruit of a thousand cows."}},{"n":143,"text":"लवेडिकां ततो गच्छेत्पुण्यां पुण्योपसेविताम् ।\nवाजपेयमवाप्नोति विमानस्थश्च पूज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one should go to holy Lavedika, frequented by the righteous; one gains the Vajapeya and is honoured seated in a celestial chariot."}}]}]}